ml","https://github.com/pypa/advisory-database/tree/main/vulns/tornado/PYSEC-2026-140.yaml"],"description":"Tornado is vulnerable to DoS due to too many multipart parts","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","metrics":{"baseScore":7.5,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":3.6},"vendorMetadata":{}},{"type":"Secondary","version":"4.0","vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","metrics":{"baseScore":8.7},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-31958","epss":0.00375,"percentile":0.31345,"date":"2026-09-20"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-31958","cwe":"CWE-400","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["6.5.5"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"6.5.5","date":"2026-03-12","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.2925},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-31958","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-31958","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"High","urls":["https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-qjxf-f2mg-c6mc","https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2026/04/msg00000.html"],"description":"Tornado is a Python web framework and asynchronous networking library. In versions of Tornado prior to 6.5.5, the only limit on the number of parts in multipart/form-data is the max_body_size setting (default 100MB). Since parsing occurs synchronously on the main thread, this creates the possibility of denial-of-service due to the cost of parsing very large multipart bodies with many parts. This vulnerability is fixed in 6.5.5.","cvss":[{"source":"nvd@nist.gov","type":"Primary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","metrics":{"baseScore":7.5,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":3.6},"vendorMetadata":{}},{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","version":"4.0","vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/S